<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Louis came in without an appointment with a sore throat, a runny and blocked nose and a dry cough for three days, after a friend he visited had a cold. He has felt warm but has had no shaking chills, no shortness of breath, no chest pain and no pain over the face or teeth. He has taken aripiprazole 5 mg each morning for two weeks without side effects, and his persecutory fears have eased; he has had no cocaine since three days before his intake visit, and his contingency management urine tests have been negative. He wanted to buy a decongestant from the pharmacy and asked whether it was safe. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Onset</td><td>Three days ago</td></tr><tr><td>Location</td><td>Throat and nose</td></tr><tr><td>Duration</td><td>Three days</td></tr><tr><td>Character</td><td>Scratchy throat, clear nasal discharge, dry cough</td></tr><tr><td>Severity</td><td>Mild to moderate; sleeping less well</td></tr><tr><td>Timing</td><td>Constant, cough worse at night</td></tr><tr><td>Context</td><td>Sick contact; on aripiprazole; blood pressure not yet treated</td></tr><tr><td>Modifying factors</td><td>Warm drinks help</td></tr><tr><td>Associated signs and symptoms</td><td>Feels warm; no shortness of breath, chest pain or facial pain</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
